    <h2 id="how-to-use-heading">How to Use This Tool — Step by Step</h2>
    <ol class="irm-steps-list">
      <li>
        <strong>Step 1 — Locate your 2024 tax return (Form 1040).</strong> Find Line 11 for your Adjusted Gross Income (AGI) and Line 2a for tax-exempt interest income.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Step 2 — Calculate your Modified Adjusted Gross Income (MAGI).</strong> Add Line 11 (AGI) and Line 2a (tax-exempt interest) together to find your Medicare MAGI.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Step 3 — Select your tax filing status in the calculator.</strong> Choose Single, Married Filing Jointly, or Married Filing Separately.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Step 4 — Click "Calculate My IRMAA Surcharge."</strong> View your exact Part B and Part D surcharge tiers and total combined monthly payment for 2026.
      </li>
    </ol>

    <!-- Pro Tip -->
    <div class="irm-pro-tip-box">
      <p class="irm-pro-tip-title">💡 Pro Tip — Lower Your IRMAA Surcharge with Form SSA-44</p>
      <p class="irm-pro-tip-text">
        If your 2024 income was high because you were still working, but you retired or had a qualifying life-changing event in 2025 or 2026, you do not have to pay the higher IRMAA rate! File Form SSA-44 with Social Security to request an immediate reduction. Use our <a href="/tools/irmaa-appeal-letter-generator/">IRMAA appeal letter generator</a> to create your custom appeal packet.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════
