  <!-- ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════
       TERMINOLOGIES / ABBREVIATIONS GLOSSARY (Rule 21)
       ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════ -->
  <section class="irm-section" aria-labelledby="terms-heading">
    <h2 id="terms-heading">Important Terminologies &amp; Abbreviations Explained</h2>
    <div class="irm-terms-grid">
      <div class="irm-term-item">
        <strong>IRMAA (Income Related Monthly Adjustment Amount)</strong>
        <p>A higher monthly surcharge added to Medicare Part B and Part D premiums for individuals with higher income.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="irm-term-item">
        <strong>MAGI (Modified Adjusted Gross Income)</strong>
        <p>Your IRS Adjusted Gross Income (AGI) plus tax-exempt interest income. Social Security uses this figure to determine your IRMAA tier.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="irm-term-item">
        <strong>Part B</strong>
        <p>Medicare medical insurance covering doctor visits and outpatient care. Standard 2026 premium is $202.90/month.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="irm-term-item">
        <strong>Part D</strong>
        <p>Medicare prescription drug coverage. High earners pay an extra Part D IRMAA surcharge on top of their plan premium.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="irm-term-item">
        <strong>SSA Form SSA-44</strong>
        <p>The official Social Security form used to appeal an IRMAA surcharge after experiencing a qualifying life-changing event.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="irm-term-item">
        <strong>CMS (Centers for Medicare &amp; Medicaid Services)</strong>
        <p>The federal government agency that establishes annual IRMAA income brackets and Medicare premium rates.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

